 "title": "Acid Lead",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: the acid squelch an octave up, as a screaming, sliding lead line: resonant, rubbery, echoing.\n\nHow it's built: a saw with its pitch through a Slew (legato notes slide) into the Ladder filter with RESONANCE high; an envelope squelches the CUTOFF on each note; Drive for grit; a Delay with plenty of feedback. One voice.\n\nPlay: fast lines, overlapping notes for slides; ride the CUTOFF with a knob (LEARN).\n\nTweak: CUTOFF, RESONANCE, the filter's CV and the envelope's DECAY, the delay's FEEDBACK.",
